      ]
    },
    "Accounting": {
      "objects": [
        "Accountant",
        "Financial Record",
        "Tuition Fee",
        "Payment Reminder"
      ]
    }
  }
}
```

#### Task:
- Assign the subdomains to bounded contexts. 
- Name the subdomain the bounded context might be derived from, it might also be multiple.
- Identify cases, where an object does not have a unified meaning across all bounded contexts and suggest a name change.
- Return the bounded contexts in json format. Here is an example for structuring the data:
```json
{
  "bounded contexts": {
    "...": {
      "derived from": "...",
      "objects": [
        "...",
        "..."
      ],
      "name changes": []
    },
    "...": {
      "derived from": "...",
      "objects": [
        "...",
        "...",
        "..."
      ],
      "name changes": [
        "... -> ..."
      ]
    }
  }
}
```

Here are the bounded contexts: 
```json
{
  "bounded contexts": {
    "Grading": {
      "derived from": "Grading Subdomain",
      "objects": [
        "Grader",
        "Assignment",
        "Exam"
      ],
      "name changes": [
        "Lecturer -> Grader"
      ]
    },
    "Admission": {
      "derived from": "Admission Subdomain",
      "objects": [
        "Applicant",
        "Application Form",
        "Required Documents",
        "Registrar",
        "Admission Committee",
        "Enrollment Record"
      ],
      "name changes": [
        "Student -> Applicant"
      ]
    },
    "Studies": {
      "derived from": "Studies Subdomain",
